  "title": "Kourovka problem 20.52 (main)",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "pdf-text-entry",
    "text": "A famous result of Burnside states that if k(G) is the number of conjugacy\nclasses of a finite group G of odd order, then |G| − k(G) is divisible by 16. Is it true\nthat for every integer m > 0 there exists a finite non-abelian group G(m) of odd order\nsuch that |G(m)| − k(G(m)) = 16m?                                          D. MacHale",
